   "confidence": "documented",
   "confidence_note": "The eviction and demolition counts come from Malaysian press reports, and the figure of 151 homes is Free Malaysia Today's account of another report rather than a government count. The project team, Malaysia Rail Link and China Communications Construction (ECRL), told Malaysiakini that Kampung Sungai Salak had flooded for close to a decade before its works began, that it had received no official complaint of cracked walls, and that it chose bored piling to keep vibration and noise down. A year later the Selangor chief minister said the flash floods had resulted from the construction and that the company would pay for blasting damage (Selangor Journal). The claims in the 2026 High Court case have not been tested. The chief minister also said in February 2024 that outsiders were inciting residents against the project (Free Malaysia Today).",
