   "fields_add": {
    "conditions": " AidData's record, read on 15 November 2026, states that the loan was secured against SOGES S.A.'s future electricity sales receipts and against a minimum cash balance in a lender-controlled escrow account, starting at US$20 million and rising to US$90 million, which the borrower was expected to reach by March 2021. Guinea covered the 15% of project cost it had to fund itself by selling its 51% stake in SOGEKA, the company running the Kaleta dam, to China Three Gorges for US$200 million (AidData, record 187)."
